The error is in the `test_device_init_level` test case. The test drivers used to verify initialization levels are recording the wrong level values. The initialization functions `my_driver_lv_1_init` and `my_driver_lv_3_init` have their level values swapped.

`my_driver_level_3` is initialized at `PRE_KERNEL_1`, so its init function `my_driver_lv_3_init` should record `LEVEL_PRE_KERNEL_1`.
`my_driver_level_1` is initialized at `POST_KERNEL`, so its init function `my_driver_lv_1_init` should record `LEVEL_POST_KERNEL`.

The fix is to swap the values assigned to `init_level_sequence` in these two functions to match their respective initialization levels.

